  <Typographies>
    <!--
      READ BEFORE ADDING A LANGUAGE OR EDITING THESE THREE TYPOGRAPHIES.

      Poppins_SemiBold_60, Poppins_Light_60 and Poppins_Medium_40 carry
      DELIBERATELY NARROW WildcardCharacters sets instead of full ASCII,
      because glyph bitmaps are image RAM on this target and these are the
      three largest fonts in the app. Every field that reaches them was
      traced:

        Light_60, Medium_40   TwoTonePicker valSep / valLeft / valRight /
                              valFracLo / nextVal, written from PickerLogic
                              with "%02u" and "%u" and a literal "." or ":".
                              Digits only, coupled to nothing.
        SemiBold_60           the same picker fields, plus TrackFaceStatus
                              dayTimeValue "%u:%02u", TrackLapView and
                              TrackHoldConfirmationView timeValue "%u" and
                              "%u:%02u", TrackIntervalsCountdownView
                              timeValue "%u", and IntervalsTimer timerText
                              "%02u:%02u" / "%05.02f" / "%05.01f".

      THE TRAP: IntervalsTimer also writes timerText with "%s" of
      TypedText(T_TEXT_OPEN). That is a TRANSLATED string, so the four
      letters "Open" in the set below exist only to render it, and they are
      coupled to its translation. It is the ONLY letter path into any of
      these three fonts, and it shows on the intervals track face and the
      intervals alert screen - nowhere else.

      So: adding a language, or editing the TEXT_OPEN translation, MUST add
      the new letters here. That coupling is DECLARED in
      wildcard-requirements.json beside this file and checked by apps-ci
      (Utilities/Scripts/app_packer/validate_wildcards.py), so it fails the
      build rather than rendering as the '?' fallback at 60px.

      Keep the declaration in step with reality. The check verifies what it
      is told; it cannot see a new code path for itself. If some other code
      starts writing into one of these widgets, add the Text id there.

      The space is in every set on purpose. It is a zero-width bitmap and one
      GlyphNode, and leaving it out is the easiest way to break this: any
      later "%s: %u" style format would render its space as '?'.

      SummaryFaceLaps has a widget ALSO called timerText which renders
      "Total: h:mm:ss" - it is T_TMP_REGULAR_18, full ASCII, and unaffected.
      Said here because the name collision has already misled one reading of
      this code.
    -->
    <Typography Id="Poppins_Regular_18" Font="Poppins-Regular.ttf" Size="18" Bpp="4" IsVector="no" Direction="LTR" FallbackCharacter="?" WildcardCharacters="! \&quot;#$%&amp;\'()*+,-./0123456789:;&lt;=&gt;?@ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ[\\]^_`abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz{|}~…" EllipsisCharacter="…" />
